// GloCo_Users_AreaBaseline — one row per user who has ever submitted a piece of case work (review, triage or admin
// finalise), with the date of their most recent submission and how many days ago that was.
// A baseline of who in each area has used the Case Review / Work Management apps for real, and who has gone quiet.
//
// POPULATION: users credited with at least one submitted piece of work in GloCo_CaseReview_Activity, all time:
// a review (incl. early advice), triage or admin finalise with Status == "Submitted". Streamlined threshold tests
// are excluded: they have no submission step (the Activity function always leaves them "Started"). Triage counts
// "adjusted": a triage submission inferred for a period capture was down qualifies, dated at its start (see
// GloCo_CaseReview_Activity, TAINT). Reviews and triage started but never submitted do not qualify. Work nobody
// was signed in for is credited to no one and is not listed.
//
// COLUMNS
//   Area                      the user's area AT THEIR LAST SUBMISSION (User_AreaOrCPSD of that piece of work,
//                             so CPS Direct shows as "CPSD"); "(unknown)" when none was ever captured.
//   Username                  email, as credited on that piece of work.
//   Last submission           date (UTC) of the most recent submission, yyyy-MM-dd.
//   Last submission (days ago) whole calendar days from that date to today; 0 = today.
//
// TIME: all history, via GloCo_CaseReview_Activity's launch-date floor; the Log Analytics time picker still
// bounds the tables read, so set it to cover launch when running this by name.
//
// Contains no PII itself (it is committable); its OUTPUT contains email addresses.
GloCo_CaseReview_Activity
| where Status == "Submitted"
| where isnotempty(User_ObjectId) and isnotempty(User_Email)
| summarize arg_max(SubmittedAt, User_Email, User_AreaOrCPSD) by User_ObjectId
| project Area = coalesce(User_AreaOrCPSD, "(unknown)"),
          Username = User_Email,
          ["Last submission"] = format_datetime(SubmittedAt, "yyyy-MM-dd"),
          ["Last submission (days ago)"] = datetime_diff("day", startofday(now()), startofday(SubmittedAt))
| order by Area asc, ["Last submission (days ago)"] asc, Username asc
